{
  "version": 51,
  "issued_at": "2026-08-13T19:00:00Z",
  "comment": "Policy 51, DEV CHANNEL ONLY. Points at drawbridge 0.2.8 build 25 and herald 0.1.11, both from v0.2.8-dev.2, which is a pre-release deliberately not flagged latest so main goes on resolving herald 0.1.9 through v0.2.5. Policy content is unchanged from 49; only the two fields that name builds moved. What the builds fix, all found by running the previous one on a phone: herald polled main's policy while drawbridge polled dev's, so one handset ran two apps against two documents; Shorts did not unwind when tapped inside YouTube, because that is a pushState and the Kotlin rewrite only sees navigations; and allowing an app did not bring it back, because the restore subtracted blocked_packages from its own candidates and an option exempts without unlisting.",
